{"text": "ALEXIS\n\nemail@gmail.com - 123-456-7890 - linkedinprofile.com\n\nExperience\nLocal Convention Centre September 2017 - present\nMeeting Manager\nI manage the logistical and food & beverage elements of the meetings and special events markets.\n\nManage all aspects of assigned meetings, conferences, and special events of up to 2,000\nattendees, while complying with internal requirements and aligning with Centre\u2019s business\npractices.\nProvide room setup and move-in/out suggestions to clients to ensure a successful event &\nmaintain fire code regulations.\nSuggest catering menus & additional services within clients\u2019 budgets that will enhance their\nevent.\nWork with clients to ensure event details are gathered in a timely manner and reflect company\u2019s\nbest practices.\nEffectively manage communication of event details to internal and external business partners,\nvendors, and suppliers.\nUtilize relationship management skills to troubleshoot any unique requests or onsite concerns\nfrom clients.\nObtain post-event feedback and evaluations from clients.\nEnsure invoices are accurate and provided to clients by the service standard timeline.\nProvide accurate and timely food & beverage revenue forecasting for all events assigned.\n\nLocal Convention Centre June 2016 - September 2017\nEvent Coordinator\nI coordinated the logistical elements of the conventions, tradeshows and meetings that take place.\n\ne Planned logistical and food & beverage details for internal & external meetings.\ne Answered general public & client inquiries about facility via verbal and written\ncommunication. Identified and escalated any concerns to appropriate managers or\ndepartments.\nLead site visits of the facility for clients.\nOn-site venue contact for clients during their event to ensure their on-site requests were\nactioned immediately.\ne Provided training and guidance to new staff members and co-op students.\ne Supported two event managers and a meeting manager.\ne Worked within a team to implement changes to the Centre\u2019s Operating Guidelines across the\norganization. Organized a 4-day training for staff members on the Operating Guidelines.\n\nInternational Documentary Film Festival February - May 2016\nEvents Associate\nPart of a small team that coordinated 60+ events, leading up to and during the Festival.\n\ne Lead planner on 4 events.\ne Trained and managed event volunteers.\ne Assisted with maintaining key sponsor & industry relationships.",
